### AGENTS.md > Athlete data, and what gets tracked in git
## Athlete data, and what gets tracked in git

- Anything with athlete identifiers does not belong in this repo, not even gitignored.
  Gitignoring it means it exists on one machine only. Put it on the primary storage
  drive, which both machines sync and GitHub never sees, and point at it from
  `data/README.md`.
- Aggregate output is different. Charts of counts, rates, and group distributions carry
  no identifiers, so track them in git and both machines get them.
- Before committing any image, open it and confirm no athlete name appears in a label.
  A per-athlete chart is athlete data and goes on the drive.

